      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>The insurer's engineer surveyor keeps people safe and keeps the risk honest. A crane with no thorough examination, or a pressure vessel outside its written scheme, can lead to a serious loss. The tool you pick should get your examination, and any dangerous defect, recorded accurately while you are still on site.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>There are two main regimes: LOLER 1998 for lifting equipment and PSSR 2000 for pressure systems.</li><li>Both examinations are duties, done by a competent person.</li><li>Under LOLER regulation 10, a defect that is or could become a danger to people must be notified to the employer forthwith. Where there is an existing or imminent risk of serious personal injury, a copy of the report goes to the enforcing authority.</li><li>The written scheme sets what is examined, how and when. The report ties back to it.</li><li>Photos and severity recorded on the spot beat notes written later.</li><li>Quickler records the examination and writes the report. It does not certify the plant. You do.</li></ul>"
    },
